 {
  "id": "c048",
  "loc_a": "formal/PROPERTIES.md:211-212",
  "quote_a": "Ship and the\n      refusal trigger deliberately overlap at now = declared+Delta — an\n      intentional boundary race, named in the module.",
  "loc_b": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-2.md:150-160",
  "quote_b": "The\n   wall-side boundary is **resolved by the latch, not raced** (round-3\n   repair, 2026-07-21: an earlier draft of this paragraph carried the\n   fused-clock race forward; under latched eligibility there is none).\n   Eligibility observed at exactly `B = declared + δ + S` is timely — the\n   boundary is **inclusive and latch-winning**, matching the mechanized\n   form (`burialAtWall <= declared + Delta + Slack` in the `_Latch`\n   companion) — so such an attempt latches eligible/finalizing and cannot\n   expire. Expiry (on the final attempt, refusal) applies only **strictly\n   after** the boundary, and only to attempts with no timely-latched\n   eligibility.",
  "kind": "stale_referent",
  "explanation": "A2.1 replaces the fused-clock boundary race with latched, inclusive eligibility, but the tracker still describes the overlap as an intentional race. The later clock-boundary decision did not cause the stale tracker sentence to be re-read or corrected."
 },
 {
  "id": "c049",
  "loc_a": "formal/PROPERTIES.md:126-129",
  "quote_a": "**Design-time finding routed to the A2 review\n      rounds:** A2.1's \"The rule\" sentence states conjunct 3 only; under\n      decoupled clocks conjunct 3 does not imply conjunct 2, so the\n      issuer must evaluate the full VALID_STRICT at ship (the bridge's\n      Ship does; A2.1's prose should say so).",
  "loc_b": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-7.md:156-161",
  "quote_b": "**Instrument.** A3 §A3.7.3's panel-driven repair governs: the issuer\n   ships on the three temporal conjuncts of A2 §A2.2 plus burial depth\n   `DepthK = k − 1`, and does not re-run envelope verification (P1–P3)\n   at ship. The §A3.9 summary line \"A2.1 prose repair (issuer ships on\n   full `VALID_STRICT`)\" (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-3.md:832`) is\n   the unrepaired wording and is superseded; it is not edited.",
  "kind": "stale_referent",
  "explanation": "The tracker retains the superseded full-`VALID_STRICT` ship obligation and attributes it to the bridge model, while A7.6 limits the guard to three temporal conjuncts plus burial depth and expressly excludes P1-P3 re-evaluation."
 },
 {
  "id": "c050",
  "loc_a": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:211-213",
