  "id": "c075",
  "loc_a": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-11.md:109-113",
  "quote_a": "1. **H3 (`phase-0-prereg.md:232-248`): not amended.** H3 is a hypothesis with a stated falsifier. Its examples are AWS-based, but they do not restrict it to AWS. It is measured over the whole deployed system, every provider included. A measurement protocol is recorded before measurement. It covers retained resources (including the compliance-locked trail bucket), defines the demonstration and idle periods, and reports the three numbers separately.",
  "loc_b": "docs/phase-0-prereg.md:244-248",
  "quote_b": "Cost is measured against *standard* pricing, not free-tier: free-tier credits may cover actual spend, but H3 evidences cost *governance*, not subsidy. *Falsified if:* a measured demo cycle exceeds $25 at standard rates, the persistent footprint exceeds $5/month, or any idle compute persists between demonstrations.",
  "kind": "silent_change",
  "explanation": "A11.5 item 1 says H3 is \"not amended\" but adds a pre-measurement protocol requirement that H3 does not contain; A11.3 does not list phase-0-prereg.md:232-248 as changed."
