  "loc_a": "docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1297-1298",
  "quote_a": "7. **Spec revocation text.** SPEC R-5.21 (1358) requires the revocation conjunct for `VALID_STRICT`. A9.4 and A9.7 rows\n   7 to 9 replace it for V1. Not a defect; listed so an implementer does not read the spec alone.",
  "loc_b": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:255-258",
  "quote_b": "- **Weakened.** For V1 bundles, `VALID_STRICT` evaluates neither P6 condition: `key_authorized(declared_issue_time)`\n  against effective revocation, and no revocation effective at or before `max(anchor_time, declared_issue_time)`\n  (A4.3). Every report carries `revocation: NOT_EVALUATED` next to the verdict. *Why:* under the registered text\n  a verifier that cannot evaluate revocation returns `UNVERIFIABLE` for every receipt.",
  "kind": "silent_change",
  "explanation": "A9.4 removes the revocation conjunct that SPEC R-5.21 requires for `VALID_STRICT`, but A9.7 rows 7-9 do not list that SPEC sentence. The required change table therefore remains incomplete even though the profile identifies the governing rule."
 },
