 {
  "id": "c086",
  "loc_a": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:266-269",
  "quote_a": "A later verifier given a V1 bundle, under the same governing V1 specification, policy, trust configuration and other declared inputs, returns the same verdict and values in the stable field set (A9.1), and never a weaker verdict because of missing status capture.",
  "loc_b": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-11.md:81-83",
  "quote_b": "**An implementation-conformance defect** (the verifier disagrees with the governing specification, for example by accepting a malformed or prohibited case the specification rejects, A9:278) is not preserved as V1 behaviour. It is fixed in a signed release, which names the affected releases and says what changed.",
  "kind": "verdict",
  "explanation": "For a bundle that exercises a conformance defect the original release wrongly accepted, the fixed release returns a different verdict on exactly the same declared inputs, contradicting A9.4's unconditional same-verdict contract; A9.4's stated carve-outs (missing status capture, append-only trust configurations, later algorithm policy) do not cover verifier defects, and A11.3 lists no change to A9:266-269."
 },
 {
