 {
  "id": "c088",
  "loc_a": "formal/p8/PROOF.md:134",
  "quote_a": "An OpenPGP signature as GnuPG emits it carries OpenPGP's own SHA-1 issuer fingerprint in a subpacket. Those\n    bytes are committed in `A_sig` like the rest, but no V1 check reads them.",
  "loc_b": "docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1105",
  "quote_b": "validation, in the hashed area: at most one type-16 subpacket, with exactly 8 data octets; at most one type-33\n    subpacket, with exactly 21 data octets whose first octet is `04` (v4 fingerprint); if both are present, the\n    type-16 value equals the last 8 octets of the type-33 fingerprint. Otherwise `INVALID / SIG_POLICY`.",
  "kind": "stale_referent",
  "explanation": "The profile requires reading fingerprint bytes to check their version and consistency with the issuer key ID. PROOF retains the broader assertion that no V1 check reads those bytes, rather than merely saying they confer no key-binding authority."
 },
 {
