  "quote_a": "   unchanged.** (K-R) itself stands: the ML-DSA-65 key signs only V1 tagged strings, in pure mode with the empty\n   context, under EXTERNAL_MU, for no other protocol. What changes is who enforces it. The supplement names the\n   issuer as the computer of `μ` and the issuer role as the only `kms:Sign` principal. In V1 as designed (deployment pending), a\n   dedicated policy signer validates the complete frame (tag, alg, key fingerprint, ε, `sign_by`, the signing stop)\n   *before* computing `μ`, and its role is the only `kms:Sign` principal (`service/signer-kms/`; key policy in",
  "loc_b": "formal/p8/HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT.md:495",
  "quote_b": "   - Stated limit: manifests carry no declared time, so the ε check does not apply to possession signing; C3 holds.",
  "kind": "other",
  "explanation": "(K-R) covers both attestation and manifest-possession frames (F ∈ Frm(attest) ∪ Frm(manifest), HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT.md:151) and only service/signer-kms/'s role holds kms:Sign, yet A11.5 item 5 states without qualification that the KMS policy signer validates ε before computing μ even though manifest frames carry no declared_issue_time."
 },
 {
  "id": "c109",
  "loc_a": "formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md:557",
  "quote_a": "The issuer obtains `S_kms` (attestation and possession) from KMS with `MessageType EXTERNAL_MU` only, sending",
