 {
  "id": "c117",
  "loc_a": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-11.md:147-150",
  "quote_a": "5. **K-R's enforcement (`formal/p8/HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT.md:148-172, :533`): amended in wording, the assumption\n   unchanged.** (K-R) itself stands: the ML-DSA-65 key signs only V1 tagged strings, in pure mode with the empty\n   context, under EXTERNAL_MU, for no other protocol. What changes is who enforces it. The supplement names the\n   issuer as the computer of `μ` and the issuer role as the only `kms:Sign` principal.",
  "loc_b": "formal/p8/HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT.md:173-174",
  "quote_b": "- So (K-R) is an issuer-code and IAM assumption: the key policy grants `kms:Sign` only to the issuer role, and the\n  issuer code builds only V1 frames. It is not an HSM property. The operations runbook carries the key policy.",
  "kind": "wrong_citation",
  "explanation": "A11.5 item 5 cites HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT.md:148-172, :533 for the supplement's enforcement statement, omitting lines 173-174 where the supplement actually states that the key policy grants kms:Sign only to the issuer role (and A11.3:93 cites :151-152, :173-174, :533, cutting off line 153 where \"computed by the issuer\" appears)."
 },
 {
  "id": "c118",
  "loc_a": "formal/p8/HYBRID-SUPPLEMENT.md:173-174",
  "quote_a": "- So (K-R) is an issuer-code and IAM assumption: the key policy grants `kms:Sign` only to the issuer role, and the\n  issuer code builds only V1 frames. It is not an HSM property. The operations runbook carries the key policy.",
  "loc_b": "service/issuer/DEPLOY.md:50-54",
  "quote_b": "5. **KMS signer.** `terraform -chdir=../signer-kms/infra plan` with the issuer's queue and bucket outputs,\n   `kms_key_id`, `key_fp` and `trail_retention_days`. The retention has no default, because Object Lock COMPLIANCE\n   retention can never be shortened; choose it here. The plan **replaces the key's whole policy**: the account root\n   keeps key administration (including `PutKeyPolicy`), only the signer role may `kms:Sign`, and everyone else is\n   explicitly denied it. Read that diff, then apply.",
  "kind": "stale_referent",
  "explanation": "The frozen supplement makes the issuer role the sole `kms:Sign` principal, whereas deployment makes a dedicated signer role the only signing principal and denies everyone else. A11.5 acknowledges that this changes the registered text, but no signed amendment has resolved it."
 },
 {
  "id": "c119",
  "loc_a": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-11.md:141-144",
