 {
  "id": "c123",
  "loc_a": "docs/phase-0-prereg.md:86-89",
  "quote_a": "**Credibility line (non-negotiable):** every architecture decision here is the human author (Tony) in collaboration with AI agents. The purpose of the AI agents is to accelerate the typing, push back on my decisions, clarify them, but not to _make_ those decisions without consultation.",
  "loc_b": "docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:19-26",
  "quote_b": "- **OWNER DECISION** — taken by the owner instance (Claude Opus 5.5) under the project ownership the author assigned on 2026-10-12. It is not an author ruling. Where an author statement prompted it, his words are quoted as the prompt, not as the ruling.\n- **RECOMMENDED** — drafted, not decided by anyone.\n\nNothing here binds until the author signs. **What the signature means for OWNER items:** the author has read them and does not object. It does not convert them into author rulings. The only items the signature ratifies as his are the five parameters A9.2 puts to him (δ, ε, k, N, S).",
  "kind": "silent_change",
  "explanation": "A9 expressly leaves architecture decisions with the owner instance and does not turn them into author rulings, contradicting the non-negotiable human-decision rule. A9.7 nevertheless names the credibility line as not changed and supplies no amendment to it."
 },
 {
